/** @page linenoisereleasehistory linenoise Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    This module is always delivered with %Qore and therefore mirrors the %Qore version.

    @section linenoise_3_0 linenoise Module Version 3.0
    - the module is delivered with %Qore and versions with it; it was a separate module, last released as version
      1.0.1
    - lines are edited with the Linenoise-NG library instead of Steve Bennett's linenoise fork
    - <b>the completion callback completes the word at the cursor</b>: the callback set with
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_callback() "set_callback()" receives the text of the line up to the cursor, and each
      string that it returns replaces the word before the cursor, which starts after the last space or other break
      character, such as \c "(", \c "=" or \c ":"; it received the whole line, and each string that it returned
      replaced the whole line (see @ref qore_3_0_0_compatibility "Changes That Can Affect Backwards-Compatibility")
    - the completion callback receives its input as a UTF-8 string, a change of the callback while a completion is
      running is safe, and the handling of exceptions raised by the callback is improved
    - added @ref Qore::Linenoise::rows() "rows()", which gives the height of the terminal
    - an external history manager can provide the history for the arrow keys and incremental search with an
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::AbstractHistoryProvider "AbstractHistoryProvider" set with
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_history_provider() "set_history_provider()"
    - new editing features:
      - syntax highlighting: @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_syntax_callback() "set_syntax_callback()"
      - a right-aligned prompt: @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_right_prompt() "set_right_prompt()"
      - inline hints: @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_hints_callback() "set_hints_callback()"
      - automatic dedent of closing characters: @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_auto_dedent() "set_auto_dedent()"
      - masked input: @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_mask_mode() "set_mask_mode()"
      - key bindings: @ref Qore::Linenoise::bind_key() "bind_key()" and
        @ref Qore::Linenoise::unbind_key() "unbind_key()"
      - a pre-filled edit buffer: @ref Qore::Linenoise::preload_buffer() "preload_buffer()"
      - input with a timeout: @ref Qore::Linenoise::line_with_timeout() "line_with_timeout()", which raises
        \c LINENOISE-TIMEOUT-ERROR
      - undo with \c Ctrl+_, an overwrite mode with the \c Insert key, bracketed paste, and keyboard macros
    - new completion options:
      - cycling through the completions: @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_menu_complete() "set_menu_complete()"
      - case-insensitive completion:
        @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_completion_case_insensitive() "set_completion_case_insensitive()"
      - filename completion when no callback is set:
        @ref Qore::Linenoise::set_filename_completion() "set_filename_completion()"
    - new asynchronous line editing API for event loops: @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_start() "edit_start()",
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_feed() "edit_feed()", @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_get_line() "edit_get_line()",
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_stop() "edit_stop()", @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_fd() "edit_fd()",
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_get_buffer() "edit_get_buffer()",
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_set_silent() "edit_set_silent()" and
      @ref Qore::Linenoise::edit_key_type() "edit_key_type()"
    - @ref Qore::Linenoise::history_save() "history_save()" and @ref Qore::Linenoise::history_load() "history_load()"
      have the \c FILESYSTEM functional domain and respect its parse option
      (@ref Qore::PO_NO_FILESYSTEM "PO_NO_FILESYSTEM"), and are subject to the filesystem sandbox of the calling
      program: they raise \c FILESYSTEM-ACCESS-DENIED for a file the sandbox does not allow to be written or read
    - @ref Qore::Linenoise::history_save() "history_save()" and @ref Qore::Linenoise::history_load() "history_load()"
      refuse a file name with a NUL character with \c LINENOISE-HISTORY-SAVE-ERROR or
      \c LINENOISE-HISTORY-LOAD-ERROR instead of using the file named by the name cut at the NUL character

    @section linenoise_1_0_1 linenoise Module Version 1.0.1
    - updated to build with \c qpp from %Qore 1.12.4+

    @section linenoise_1_0_0 linenoise Module Version 1.0.0
    - initial release
*/
